VeridianOS: fix KIO compiler warnings (dead code, unused parameters, deprecated libxml2 call)

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build (musl, libxml2 2.15.4):

- src/core/kmountpoint.cpp: 's_mountIdCache' defined but not used
  [-Wunused-variable]. The MountIdCache struct and its Q_GLOBAL_STATIC are
  only used by the HAVE_STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE branch of
  KMountPoint::currentMountPointForUniqueId(); move them under the same
  condition. No behaviour change.
- src/core/workerinterface.cpp: 'readFilesize_t' defined but not used
  [-Wunused-function]. The static helper has no caller; remove it.
- src/kpasswdserver/kpasswdserver.cpp: unused parameter 'usertime'
  [-Wunused-parameter] (4x). It is only read under #if HAVE_X11, so mark it
  [[maybe_unused]]. No behaviour change.
- src/kioworkers/help/main.cpp, main_ghelp.cpp: 'xmlSubstituteEntitiesDefault'
  is deprecated [-Wdeprecated-declarations]. The documented replacement is the
  XML_PARSE_NOENT parser option. Every parse the help workers perform already
  passes it explicitly: KDocTools::transform() reads the document with
  xmlCtxtReadFile(..., XML_PARSE_NOENT | XML_PARSE_DTDLOAD | XML_PARSE_NONET),
  and libxslt loads stylesheets, imports and document() inputs with
  XSLT_PARSE_OPTIONS (XML_PARSE_NOENT | ...). libxml2 sets
  ctxt->replaceEntities from those options, overriding the global default, so
  the global call has no effect; remove it. No behaviour change.

